 "segments": [
  {
   "id": "bava_metzia.118a.12",
   "daf": "118a",
   "sentenceId": 11,
   "he": "אֵין שׁוֹמְעִין לוֹ. וְהָתַנְיָא: שׁוֹמְעִין לוֹ! אָמַר רַב נַחְמָן: לָא קַשְׁיָא. כָּאן בְּשֶׁלּוֹ, כָּאן בְּשֶׁל חֲבֵירוֹ.",
   "en": "§ The mishna teaches that if an employer seeks to pay his laborer with straw, the court «does not listen to him.» The Gemara asks: «But isn’t it taught» in a baraita that the court «does listen to him?» The Gemara answers: «Rav Naḥman said:» This is «not difficult.» The ruling of the mishna «here,» that the court does not listen to him, is stated «with regard to» a case of work done with the employer’s «own» property. And the ruling of the baraita «there,» that the court does listen to him, is stated «with regard to» work done with the property «of another,» and there the employer’s request is accepted."
  }
 ],
